=======================================================================
 THIRD PARTY NOTICES & DATASET ATTRIBUTION
=======================================================================

1. NWPU-RESISC45 DATASET
   This project uses the NWPU-RESISC45 benchmark for remote sensing image scene
   classification (45 classes), created at Northwestern Polytechnical University.
   The images and their original annotations are the property of their respective
   authors, who release them for research purposes only.

   Citation:
      G. Cheng, J. Han, and X. Lu, "Remote Sensing Image Scene Classification:
      Benchmark and State of the Art", Proceedings of the IEEE, vol. 105, no. 10,
      pp. 1865-1883, 2017. doi:10.1109/JPROC.2017.2675998

   The dataset is not part of this repository and must be obtained separately from
   its authors (expected under data/download/). Any use of the images remains subject
   to the terms set by the dataset authors, independently of the license above.

2. MODIFICATIONS (DERIVED LABEL SETS)
   The label sets produced by this software are DERIVATIVE WORKS of the NWPU-RESISC45
   annotations. They were deliberately corrupted for research on neural network
   robustness and MUST NOT be mistaken for the original ground truth:

      * RQ1: symmetric label noise: affected labels are reassigned uniformly at
              random across all classes.
      * RQ2: targeted semantic label flipping: labels are swapped only within
              visually similar class pairs.

   The image data itself is never modified, only labels are replaced. Poisoned labels
   are stored separately from the clean HDF5 files, under
   data/processed/resisc45/poisoned/.

   The defense experiments (RQ3) introduce no further corruption. The reactive methods
   evaluated there (e.g. loss-based sample filtering) do, however, derive filtered or
   corrected label subsets from the poisoned sets above; these are likewise not the
   original annotations.

3. SOFTWARE DEPENDENCIES
   All third-party Python packages remain under their own licenses; see
   requirements.txt for the pinned versions. The model architectures (ResNet-18,
   MobileNetV2, ConvNeXt-Tiny) are instantiated from torchvision (BSD 3-Clause) and
   trained from scratch (weights=None). No pretrained weights are redistributed here.

